WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.222
There are many vector-search tools, and students do not need to memorize every product.

00:00:06.222 --> 00:00:09.587
Instead, focus on the categories and the engineering tradeoffs.

00:00:09.587 --> 00:00:15.332
FAISS is a fast local vector-search library, but it is not a full database.

00:00:15.332 --> 00:00:18.747
Chroma is convenient for local prototypes.

00:00:18.747 --> 00:00:23.442
Qdrant is a vector database with strong metadata filtering.

00:00:23.442 --> 00:00:31.077
pgvector keeps vector search inside PostgreSQL, which can be attractive for teams already using relational

00:00:31.077 --> 00:00:34.037
data. [tts-break] Pinecone is a managed cloud service.

00:00:34.037 --> 00:00:38.982
Weaviate supports vector and hybrid search with a broader platform around it.

00:00:38.982 --> 00:00:43.682
Milvus and Zilliz are designed for larger-scale vector workloads.

00:00:43.682 --> 00:00:48.697
The syntax changes from product to product, but the pattern stays familiar:

00:00:48.697 --> 00:00:55.627
create or connect to a collection or index, insert vectors with metadata, embed the query,

00:00:55.627 --> 00:00:59.707
search for nearby vectors, and return the associated text.

00:00:59.707 --> 00:01:02.960
Choose based on the project, not on popularity.
